 ### Fixed
 
 - `onError` and `afterSession` hooks now fire when `beforeSession` throws, matching the guarantee the hook names imply. Previously, a throw from `beforeSession` escaped the `try`/`finally` block entirely, so neither hook ran. **Migration note**: if your `afterSession` hook assumed it would only be called after a full session turn, it will now also be called when `beforeSession` itself fails — the hook can inspect the session to detect this case (no entries beyond the initial user message will have been processed).
+- `onError` now fires for every rejection, including non-`Error` values. A rejection that is not already an `Error` is wrapped in one with the original value as its `cause`, so a hook typed against `Error` still compiles and a hook that needs the raw value can reach it through `error.cause`. The original rejection propagates to the caller unchanged. **Migration note**: if your `onError` hook relied on the hook never firing for non-`Error` rejections, it will now also be called for thrown strings, plain objects, or `undefined`.
 
