-## Measured semantics — out of scope
-
-This property of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` is recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue does not change it; that is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
-
-- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
+## Error-hook semantics
+
+- Every rejection invokes `onError` once with an `Error`; a non-`Error` rejection is wrapped with the original value as its `cause`, while an existing `Error` is passed through unchanged, and the original rejection still propagates to the caller ([validated by: calls onError for every rejection and preserves the caller rejection](../../src/orchestration/onErrorRejection.acceptance.test.ts#L74)).
+  - `onError` is called exactly once per non-`Error` rejection ([validated by: onError is called once for non-Error %s](../../src/orchestration/onErrorRejection.acceptance.test.ts#L75)).
+  - A non-`Error` rejection is wrapped in an `Error` instance ([validated by: non-Error %s is wrapped in an Error for onError](../../src/orchestration/onErrorRejection.acceptance.test.ts#L79)).
+  - The original non-`Error` value becomes the `cause` property on the wrapper ([validated by: non-Error %s becomes the cause on the wrapped Error](../../src/orchestration/onErrorRejection.acceptance.test.ts#L83)).
+  - The original non-`Error` rejection propagates to the caller unchanged ([validated by: caller still receives original non-Error %s unchanged](../../src/orchestration/onErrorRejection.acceptance.test.ts#L87)).
+  - `onError` is called exactly once when the provider rejects with an existing `Error` ([validated by: onError is called once for an existing Error](../../src/orchestration/onErrorRejection.acceptance.test.ts#L91)).
+  - An existing `Error` is passed to `onError` as the same instance, not a wrapper ([validated by: existing Error is passed to onError as the same instance](../../src/orchestration/onErrorRejection.acceptance.test.ts#L95)).
+  - An existing `Error` rejection propagates to the caller unchanged ([validated by: caller receives existing Error instance unchanged](../../src/orchestration/onErrorRejection.acceptance.test.ts#L99)).
